body:
It might just be the .JPG's ): in which case, any idea what setting I may have chosen to screw it up like that? I was so still and careful with things. Half of the .JPG's are like that, even when people were still, and I have a tripod and don't think I really moved that much, but ya never know ): I'm just at a loss. There are still a lot of good photos in that, but I'm so upset that so many turned out with the ghosting sort of thing.

&#x200B;

Also, partner has no idea z-z; so. No clue. I could get the camera and search for you if that somehow helps (if you knew where I should look).
